# The plan for capabilities and shape rules, written before the code.
#
# Until now the description of a module stopped at its types. A plan could not
# name a function, or a method of anything but an interface, and the invariants
# could only make rules about packages and what they import. This change lets a
# design say what the code offers and how it looks:
#
#   - gocode records every function a package exports (:func), the exported
#     methods of every type and not only an interface's (:method), each type's
#     kind (:kind), and the name each package declares (:name);
#   - a plan can name those, and conform holds the code to them both ways;
#   - the invariants can name them too, as capabilities a package, a type or a
#     whole group keeps offering, and can fix them, so that the code offers
#     nothing they do not list;
#   - the invariants' rules range over types as well as packages: what kind a
#     type is, whether it is documented, where it is defined, what it implements
#     and what it holds;
#   - a plan that states something nothing checks is told so.
#
# No type, field, package or import is new. What is below are the words the
# description gains, and the one function that lets a person read the facts a
# rule is checked against.

Prefix(:=<https://github.com/LukasSelin/gowl/self#>)
Prefix(rdfs:=<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>)

Ontology(<https://github.com/LukasSelin/gowl/design/capabilities>

    # The words the description gains.
    Declaration(AnnotationProperty(:func))
    AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment :func "A function the subject Go package exports, as Name(parameter types) result types.")
    Declaration(AnnotationProperty(:kind))
    AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment :kind "What the subject Go type is underneath: struct, interface, basic, slice, array, map, chan, func or pointer.")
    Declaration(AnnotationProperty(:name))
    AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment :name "The name the subject Go package declares, which qualifies what it exports: owl in owl.Class.")

    # The facts the invariants are checked against, for a person to read.
    Declaration(NamedIndividual(:package.gowl.internal.gocode))
    ClassAssertion(:Package :package.gowl.internal.gocode)
    AnnotationAssertion(:func :package.gowl.internal.gocode "Facts(invariants, module *owl.Ontology, known []owl.NamedIndividual) *owl.Ontology")
)
